url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7174/6563137305_833f329965_c.jpg", "title": "Euphorbia at terrace", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7166/6582374705_10aef7906e_c.jpg", "title": "Entry Gate and planters", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7023/6582046731_0d3526b8f8_c.jpg", "title": "Clematis x 'Avalanche'", "description": "A hybrid cross between two New Zealand evergreen Clematis species, paniculata and marmoraria.  This form is a selected seedling from that cross, selected and patented in England, and available through San Marcos Growers in Santa Barbara.  It has fabulous cut glossy green foliage that is showy all year round, but the pure white flowers in mass in spring are simply dazzling."}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7034/6582358887_db16171dc4_c.jpg", "title": "Aechmea 'Suenos'", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7143/6562998721_638820f8b8_c.jpg", "title": "Acanthus spinossimus in bloom", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7013/6563135281_803ed4d76c_c.jpg", "title": "Terrace off family room", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7031/6563134737_5505efd795_c.jpg", "title": "Plantings in built-in planter at kitchen balcony", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7016/6562996227_49132064ef_c.jpg", "title": "Aeonium 'Sunburst'", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7029/6581663431_f1ff049820_c.jpg", "title": "Cannomois grande in pot at upper balcony", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7007/6582363407_ded2b3bc56_c.jpg", "title": "Palms and bromeliads", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7003/6581455135_cfb7f54aec_c.jpg", "title": "Mathiasella bupleuroides", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7167/6582376585_eb1bff7e8b_c.jpg", "title": "", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7141/6582097797_52986ffed6_c.jpg", "title": "Abutilon hybrid yellow", "description": "I got this from Suncrest Wholesale Nursery, but don't remember what the cultivar name(if any) was.  It turned out to be one of the best yellow flowered types I've ever used, as it stayed dense, bloomed non-stop, and needed so little attention.  Anyone recognize it?"}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7006/6582372581_e6a02579c2_c.jpg", "title": "Aechmea recurvata v, recurvata", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7029/6582356411_4d2d5289d8_c.jpg", "title": "Aechmea 'Covata'", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7026/6581464519_c40aa93dd5_c.jpg", "title": "Banksia blechnifolia bloom", "description": "The blooms on this species tend to come at the ends of longer sprawling stems that follow the ground, or in this case, extend off into space in this third story built-in balcony planter.  Therefore it isn't really ideally suited to smaller scaled pots or manicured situations.  It works great here, where the stems put the flowers out beyond obscuring foliage, and make for an interesting view from below or the side."}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7025/6562998559_4bba1b949f_c.jpg", "title": "Arctotis 'Burgundy' in bloom", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7144/6582096985_fc9f4f2689_c.jpg", "title": "Arenga engleri and Salvia splendens 'Vanhouttii'", "description": ""}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/5054/5511341111_df1172ca3e_c.jpg", "title": "Lotus maculatus 'Gold Flash', Parrot's Beak Lotus", "description": "A wonderful spring blooming short lived perennial from the Canary Islands, that is probably best used as a filler/spiller in large pots, or temporary ground cover on slopes while your more permanent plants are filling in.  Usually only lasts for two years of growth when I've planted it."}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/5253/5511272423_e600245323_c.jpg", "title": "Nidularium innocentii", "description": "A great foliage bromeliad for a shade garden, as it colors up strongly even without bright light, and keeps this color all year round, as opposed to some of the Neoregelias or Fascicularias.  Purple and pale greens are a color combination that I particularly like, and this has it in spades."}, {"url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/7014/6581677813_4a258e603c_c.jpg", "title": "Clivia miniata aurea", "description": ""}]